--TEST--
`Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::set` throws a `RuntimeError` for each property whose `PropertyInfo::isReadonly` is `true`, writes each other public one, and writes a `lateinit` one the program has not written yet — `rule:core-classes/reflect`, `rule:security/reflection-enforces-visibility`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Reflect\PropertyInfo::isReadonly, Core\Reflect\PropertyInfo::isLateInit
class Ticket {
    public string $status = "open";
    public lateinit string $owner;

    public function constructor(public readonly string $code) {
    }
}

var $ticket = new Ticket("T-1");
var $described = Core\Reflect::forObject($ticket);
// The loop tries to write "changed" into every property.
foreach ($described->properties() as Core\Reflect\PropertyInfo $property) {
    try {
        $described->set($ticket, $property->name(), "changed");
        echo $property->name(), ' written', $property->isLateInit() ? ' (lateinit)' : '', "\n";
    } catch (RuntimeError $e) {
        echo $property->name(), ' readonly=', $property->isReadonly() ? 'yes' : 'no', ': ', $e->message, "\n";
    }
}
echo $ticket->status, ' ', $ticket->owner, ' ', $ticket->code, "\n";
--EXPECT--
status written
owner written (lateinit)
code readonly=yes: cannot modify `readonly` property `Ticket::$code`
changed changed T-1
